# Optional. Base URL for *direct* Energy-Charts requests from the browser.
#
# The public API does not send CORS headers for third-party origins, so a
# plain GitHub-Pages deployment cannot call it directly – it uses the
# snapshot in public/data/latest.json instead (refreshed by GitHub Actions).
#
# In `npm run dev` the Vite dev server proxies /api/energy-charts to the real
# API, so live mode works locally without any configuration.
#
# If you run your own CORS-enabled proxy in front of https://api.energy-charts.info
# you can point the production build at it here:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-proxy.example.org

# Optional. Override the GitHub-Pages base path (defaults to /50hz-of-grey/).
# BASE_PATH=/my-fork-name/
